# Sitemaps are generated into public/ by `sitemap:generate` every six hours.
# They are build output, not source: the catalogue files run to ~8 MB each, and
# a stale copy committed here would be deployed over the fresh one and served
# ahead of the routes — FrankenPHP answers with any real file in public/ before
# PHP is reached.
/public/sitemap*.xml

# The rule above only ever applied to files git was not already tracking, and
# public/sitemap.xml had been committed before it was written — so every
# `sitemap:generate` on the server left the working tree dirty and the next
# `git pull` refused to run. Untracked here on 28.08.2026; the root .gitignore
# already carried a one-off line for sitemap-news.xml, which is the same
# papercut patched once for the one file that hurt first.
